# EAS Build uploads the working directory as-is; without this, a locally
# generated (and possibly stale, from local `expo prebuild` / `expo run:android`
# debugging) android/ or ios/ folder would be uploaded and EAS would treat this
# as a bare-workflow project with pre-existing native code, skipping its own
# fresh prebuild - producing exactly the kind of confusing cloud build failure
# this file exists to prevent. Same idea as .gitignore's "generated native
# folders" entry, just for EAS's own upload step.
/android
/ios

# Local dev/build artifacts, never needed in the cloud build archive.
node_modules
.expo
dist
*.log

# .easignore replaces .gitignore for the upload, so repeat anything that must
# never leave this machine: signing/API secrets and local build outputs.
/secrets
/build-artifacts
.env*
